# This repository's own ignores.
#
# ⛔ It is PUBLIC. Everything below is either machine-local noise or material
# that must never be published. docs/public/README.md is the wider rule.

# -- source material this template was distilled from -----------------------
# ⛔ NEVER COMMITTED. Material of this shape holds live hostnames, account
# identifiers, credential filenames, private project names and email addresses.
# `scripts/common/check-no-secrets.sh --public` finds all of it, which is how
# it was confirmed rather than assumed.
#
# The template is a DISTILLATION. The methodology travels; the material does
# not. The directories themselves were removed once the distillation was done;
# these rules stay so the next batch cannot be staged by accident.
MEMOIRS/
Project*/
reference/
references/
reference_attachments/

# -- scratch ----------------------------------------------------------------
.tmp/
tmp/
scratch/
.scratch/
*.bak
*.orig

# -- logs -------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/

# -- secrets. Listed before any exist, so one can never be staged by accident -
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# -- agent and assistant local files ----------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# -- OS and editor noise ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ⛔ WINDOWS RESERVED DEVICE NAMES. Two different things create one as a real
# file, and neither of them is a file you meant to write:
#   1. your own redirect: 2>/dev/null under a shell that does not map it makes
#      a real file called nul, which git tracks, which breaks git stash
#      outright, and which cannot be deleted by rm or by Python;
#   2. a tool's own argument list: podman machine ssh passes
#      -o UserKnownHostsFile=NUL to its ssh, and under Git Bash that is a
#      filename, so a 99-byte NUL holding an ssh host key lands in whatever
#      directory the command ran in. Usually a repository.
# ⚠ MSYS_NO_PATHCONV does not prevent the second one: the argument never looked
# like a path. docs/conventions/shell.md section 7 carries the measurement.
nul
CON
PRN
AUX
NUL
COM[1-9]
LPT[1-9]
CON.*
PRN.*
AUX.*
NUL.*
COM[1-9].*
LPT[1-9].*

# -- DELIBERATELY COMMITTED. Do not add these. ------------------------------
# dotfiles/*/gitignore     they ship WITHOUT the leading dot on purpose:
#                          a real .gitignore there would apply to itself.
#                          dotfiles/README.md says why.
# LICENSES/*.txt           canonical SPDX texts, fetched not typed
# scripts/doctor/*         every project inherits the probe
